1
00:00:04,970 --> 00:00:07,400
Whoever does Star's missions is someone who likes Star.

2
00:00:07,400 --> 00:00:08,630
Listen up, guys.

3
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:10,970
If it's missions or paying 60,000 baht,

4
00:00:10,970 --> 00:00:12,600
I'd obviously pick the first, right?

5
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:13,900
Easier than expected.

6
00:00:14,270 --> 00:00:15,100
Been together long?

7
00:00:16,430 --> 00:00:18,870
Dad! Together? What are you talking about?

8
00:00:19,230 --> 00:00:21,100
You could tone down the niceness a bit, Din.

9
00:00:21,700 --> 00:00:23,330
But promise me,

10
00:00:23,330 --> 00:00:25,230
if it's ever too much, you have to stop.

11
00:00:25,570 --> 00:00:26,470
I promise.

12
00:00:26,470 --> 00:00:28,070
If it's ever too much, I'll stop.

13
00:00:28,070 --> 00:00:29,830
Same for you. You're the captain.

14
00:00:29,830 --> 00:00:32,770
If you let your emotions drive every play, how will you lead the team?

15
00:00:33,800 --> 00:00:35,030
I'm jealous of you and Chemi.

16
00:00:35,030 --> 00:00:38,370
Do you really like me, or is it just the promise from back then?

17
00:00:38,370 --> 00:00:40,270
At first I thought we felt the same way.

18
00:00:40,270 --> 00:00:41,280
But now I don't know.

19
00:00:41,280 --> 00:00:43,030
I have something to sort out first.

20
00:00:43,030 --> 00:00:43,770
What is it?

21
00:00:43,770 --> 00:00:45,030
It's something about me.

22
00:00:45,030 --> 00:00:46,330
You don't have to answer.

23
00:00:46,330 --> 00:00:48,930
I think your silence is answer enough.

24
00:00:48,930 --> 00:00:50,630
Not being clear is the answer, sweetie.

25
00:00:50,630 --> 00:00:52,330
If he wants you in his life,

26
00:00:52,330 --> 00:00:54,370
he'll do everything to keep you.

27
00:00:54,370 --> 00:00:56,530
If you can't say it, why not write it?

28
00:00:56,530 --> 00:00:59,000
When my dad messes up and wants to explain things to my mom,

29
00:00:59,000 --> 00:01:00,230
he writes it all down.

30
00:01:00,230 --> 00:01:02,170
Damn! Why didn't I think of that?

31
00:01:02,170 --> 00:01:04,500
You two are so close. Don't ever break up.

32
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:05,830
I won't ask for much of a dowry.

33
00:01:05,830 --> 00:01:08,400
But first, let me win Fuen over.

34
00:01:09,370 --> 00:01:10,970
I can always wait for you.

35
00:01:10,970 --> 00:01:13,030
But don't get too carried away with me.

36
00:03:18,829 --> 00:03:20,400
Chemi. / Yes?

37
00:03:20,400 --> 00:03:21,370
Where's Mom?

38
00:03:21,829 --> 00:03:23,230
Mom went out.

39
00:03:23,770 --> 00:03:26,430
But she made some food for you.

40
00:03:26,430 --> 00:03:28,100
Eat if you're hungry.

41
00:03:29,700 --> 00:03:32,030
Oh, Aof, this is Chemi, my little brother.

42
00:03:46,130 --> 00:03:47,670
If you're still single by then,

43
00:03:47,670 --> 00:03:49,400
I'll be your first boyfriend myself.

44
00:03:50,270 --> 00:03:52,370
Then promise me, Aof.

45
00:04:39,270 --> 00:04:41,200
Oh, Time, you're here?

46
00:04:41,200 --> 00:04:41,930
Mm.

47
00:04:42,430 --> 00:04:43,970
So, about our activity,

48
00:04:43,970 --> 00:04:45,000
how about a workshop?

49
00:04:46,700 --> 00:04:50,200
I don't think so. It'll overlap with the booths downstairs.

50
00:04:50,200 --> 00:04:53,100
And we've got the whole room.

51
00:04:53,100 --> 00:04:55,400
Why don't we do something that fills it?

52
00:04:56,470 --> 00:04:58,000
Fills the whole room?

53
00:04:58,770 --> 00:04:59,730
A cafe?

54
00:05:03,100 --> 00:05:03,930
Board games?

55
00:05:05,130 --> 00:05:06,370
Not games either?

56
00:05:07,300 --> 00:05:08,230
A haunted house?

57
00:05:11,600 --> 00:05:12,900
Then what?

58
00:05:17,300 --> 00:05:18,300
I've got it.

59
00:05:18,590 --> 00:05:19,300
What?

60
00:05:19,300 --> 00:05:21,470
Let's make this room a surprise for everyone.

61
00:05:21,470 --> 00:05:22,670
Sure. What is it?

62
00:05:26,100 --> 00:05:27,870
Sure. Cool. Let's do it.

63
00:05:28,730 --> 00:05:30,100
Yeah, let's.

64
00:05:34,630 --> 00:05:36,630
Mm-hmm. Makes sense.

65
00:05:36,630 --> 00:05:38,900
See? There are two exits, perfect.

66
00:06:40,030 --> 00:06:42,200
Chemi, there's something I want to say.

67
00:06:42,930 --> 00:06:44,230
I'm sorry, Chemi,

68
00:06:45,330 --> 00:06:47,430
for being so slow with everything.

69
00:06:49,430 --> 00:06:52,200
And I'm scared I'll say the wrong thing again.

70
00:06:53,730 --> 00:06:54,970
So...

71
00:07:02,130 --> 00:07:04,170
Chemi, could you take this, please?

72
00:07:07,030 --> 00:07:08,470
I spent all night writing it.

73
00:07:11,070 --> 00:07:12,830
I want you to read it.

74
00:07:23,700 --> 00:07:24,630
Okay.

75
00:08:06,300 --> 00:08:08,770
You and I need to talk.

76
00:08:24,670 --> 00:08:27,830
I'm not sure you won't hurt my brother again.

77
00:08:29,530 --> 00:08:33,730
I'm sorry. But this time I've really thought about how to change.

78
00:08:34,870 --> 00:08:37,799
And this time I'm trying to think before I talk.

79
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:40,000
Trying isn't enough.

80
00:08:40,770 --> 00:08:42,429
You have to show me.

81
00:08:48,270 --> 00:08:51,200
I don't know what the future holds,

82
00:08:52,970 --> 00:08:55,470
but whatever you promised my brother,

83
00:08:55,470 --> 00:08:57,130
if you hurt him again,

84
00:08:58,070 --> 00:08:59,400
as his brother...

85
00:09:00,270 --> 00:09:01,700
how could I face you?

86
00:09:10,930 --> 00:09:12,070
Physics.

87
00:09:12,500 --> 00:09:14,530
Do I really look that bad to you?

88
00:09:15,500 --> 00:09:17,600
You're not a bad guy.

89
00:09:17,600 --> 00:09:19,530
You just can't get your priorities straight.

90
00:09:34,570 --> 00:09:35,630
Is he picking up?

91
00:09:36,600 --> 00:09:39,200
No. I've called ten times already.

92
00:09:39,500 --> 00:09:40,870
So where is he?

93
00:09:41,730 --> 00:09:45,530
I called him on my way here. He said he was in his room.

94
00:09:46,670 --> 00:09:48,430
But he's still not here?

95
00:09:49,500 --> 00:09:52,000
Don't tell me he forgot Chemi's birthday.

96
00:09:52,000 --> 00:09:55,600
Nah. I bet he's just stuck in traffic.

97
00:09:55,600 --> 00:09:57,370
Wait for him a bit.

98
00:09:59,470 --> 00:10:00,770
I'm not waiting.

99
00:10:01,070 --> 00:10:02,300
Just blow them out.

100
00:10:04,170 --> 00:10:06,130
Come on, birthday time!

101
00:10:06,770 --> 00:10:13,370
Happy birthday to you, happy birthday to you

102
00:10:13,370 --> 00:10:19,970
Happy birthday, happy birthday, happy birthday to you

103
00:10:20,670 --> 00:10:22,000
Happy birthday!

104
00:10:22,000 --> 00:10:25,870
May you be very happy now that you're 15.

105
00:10:26,400 --> 00:10:29,670
And stop annoying me like you have the past 14 years.

106
00:10:32,130 --> 00:10:33,670
Yes, bro.

107
00:10:36,270 --> 00:10:38,270
Whoa, you call that a birthday wish?

108
00:10:39,600 --> 00:10:45,100
I hope you meet only good people and good things.

109
00:10:46,130 --> 00:10:48,500
I hope you get everything you wish for.

110
00:10:49,700 --> 00:10:51,770
Thank you, Fuen.

111
00:10:51,770 --> 00:10:54,670
I don't know what your life plans are,

112
00:10:54,670 --> 00:10:58,200
but I hope everything goes the way you want.

113
00:10:59,230 --> 00:11:01,000
Thank you, guys.

114
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:04,670
I'll make good use of all your wishes.

115
00:11:05,030 --> 00:11:05,830
Amen.

116
00:11:19,900 --> 00:11:21,300
Hey, let's cut the cake.

117
00:11:21,300 --> 00:11:22,930
Cut the cake! Cut the cake!

118
00:11:34,230 --> 00:11:36,130
I know you have your reasons,

119
00:11:36,570 --> 00:11:39,830
but you should've told everyone, not left them waiting.

120
00:11:40,870 --> 00:11:42,070
I'm sorry.

121
00:11:43,100 --> 00:11:45,330
I won't let that happen again.

122
00:11:45,700 --> 00:11:47,570
Can't you help me out this time?

123
00:11:49,230 --> 00:11:50,600
I don't trust you.

124
00:11:52,230 --> 00:11:54,570
You've never given me a reason to.

125
00:11:58,970 --> 00:12:01,830
Then why don't we wait for Chemi's answer?

126
00:12:02,930 --> 00:12:05,730
If he says no... it's over.

127
00:12:05,730 --> 00:12:07,100
No need to fight.

128
00:12:09,800 --> 00:12:11,970
So you're helping me now, Fuen?

129
00:12:13,830 --> 00:12:15,270
What do you want me to do?

130
00:12:15,830 --> 00:12:17,570
Say you want to keep going,

131
00:12:17,730 --> 00:12:18,870
but he says no.

132
00:12:19,330 --> 00:12:21,100
You want me to force him?

133
00:12:24,530 --> 00:12:26,400
But I get where Fuen's coming from.

134
00:12:26,870 --> 00:12:29,070
But if Chemi's okay with it,

135
00:12:29,800 --> 00:12:31,870
would you be okay too, Physics?

136
00:12:34,570 --> 00:12:35,930
I'm his brother.

137
00:12:36,500 --> 00:12:38,270
I have a right to worry about him.

138
00:12:39,400 --> 00:12:43,100
The only way I'll accept it is if you show me.

139
00:12:46,200 --> 00:12:47,100
Otherwise,

140
00:12:48,800 --> 00:12:50,700
I'm definitely not changing my mind.

141
00:13:16,930 --> 00:13:18,130
Chemi.

142
00:13:18,870 --> 00:13:21,630
I'm afraid I'll say the wrong thing again

143
00:13:21,630 --> 00:13:24,300
and we'll misunderstand each other even more.

144
00:13:24,300 --> 00:13:26,970
So I wrote this for you to read instead.

145
00:13:31,400 --> 00:13:33,470
When we first met,

146
00:13:34,600 --> 00:13:37,370
I thought you were so bright and cheerful.

147
00:13:38,200 --> 00:13:40,970
And I wanted to protect you the way Physics does.

148
00:13:59,570 --> 00:14:02,070
Careful, it's dangerous.

149
00:14:02,600 --> 00:14:04,470
Thank you, Aof.

150
00:14:04,900 --> 00:14:07,500
Because I love it when you smile.

151
00:14:10,870 --> 00:14:14,530
I'm sorry I never gave you a clear answer when you asked.

152
00:14:14,530 --> 00:14:17,330
But now I want to do everything right.

153
00:14:18,030 --> 00:14:20,500
Will you give me another chance?

154
00:14:20,730 --> 00:14:25,400
♪ Every day goes by, it never fades ♪

155
00:14:25,400 --> 00:14:34,030
♪ The feelings back then, the story back then, I still remember ♪

156
00:14:34,030 --> 00:14:44,300
♪ The smile you gave me, that day we sat side by side ♪

157
00:14:44,300 --> 00:14:54,570
♪ We once made a promise that we'd have each other ♪

158
00:14:54,570 --> 00:15:04,830
♪ That day everything seemed so clear, we laughed all day ♪

159
00:15:06,130 --> 00:15:07,870
Whatever, then.

160
00:15:07,870 --> 00:15:09,370
Woof, woof, woof.

161
00:15:10,870 --> 00:15:12,370
Quit messing with me.

162
00:15:16,130 --> 00:15:18,630
It's not that I won't listen to you guys.

163
00:15:20,970 --> 00:15:23,300
But I want to try one last time.

164
00:15:24,730 --> 00:15:26,670
If I still end up getting hurt,

165
00:15:30,170 --> 00:15:32,230
at least I'll be done with it for good.

166
00:15:34,770 --> 00:15:39,430
Then next time something's up, you tell us.

167
00:15:39,430 --> 00:15:43,130
Or I'll cry if you're hurting and we're not there for you.

168
00:15:45,530 --> 00:15:47,230
I'm telling you,

169
00:15:47,230 --> 00:15:50,900
if Aof makes you cry even one more time,

170
00:15:50,900 --> 00:15:55,170
I swear, I'll kick a ball right in his face.

171
00:15:55,170 --> 00:15:56,830
And I'll bite his ear too.

172
00:16:01,070 --> 00:16:03,130
I freaking love you guys.

173
00:16:03,830 --> 00:16:05,170
Just like that.

174
00:16:05,930 --> 00:16:09,800
Looks like the football club's got its own couple.

175
00:16:09,800 --> 00:16:10,900
Whoa.

176
00:16:10,900 --> 00:16:13,600
Who'd dare boss you around now? / Right.

177
00:16:13,600 --> 00:16:15,630
Your boyfriend's the team captain.

178
00:16:15,630 --> 00:16:18,970
Easy, guys. I haven't decided yet.

179
00:16:48,500 --> 00:16:49,630
What's on your mind?

180
00:16:49,630 --> 00:16:50,900
Yeah, what?

181
00:16:50,900 --> 00:16:52,370
About Din?

182
00:16:53,570 --> 00:16:55,200
Hmm... sure.

183
00:16:55,200 --> 00:16:56,930
So? Spill it.

184
00:16:58,270 --> 00:16:59,400
Din.

185
00:16:59,400 --> 00:17:01,500
Did you take Star home?

186
00:17:01,930 --> 00:17:03,230
And what about Rei?

187
00:17:03,230 --> 00:17:05,470
Ugh, no idea.

188
00:17:06,730 --> 00:17:08,869
I just don't get it.

189
00:17:09,500 --> 00:17:11,599
Din wants my LINE ID, right?

190
00:17:11,599 --> 00:17:13,500
But why go to so much trouble?

191
00:17:13,500 --> 00:17:16,700
I told him he didn't have to go this far.

192
00:17:19,400 --> 00:17:21,470
You took him all the way home

193
00:17:21,470 --> 00:17:23,800
just to get Star's contact?

194
00:17:26,130 --> 00:17:27,329
Because Din likes Star.

195
00:17:27,329 --> 00:17:28,400
Correct.

196
00:17:28,730 --> 00:17:31,300
Stop it! Yesterday,

197
00:17:31,300 --> 00:17:34,900
I told Din not to wait for me after class. I'd go home myself.

198
00:17:34,900 --> 00:17:37,900
But he waited till I was done, set on taking me home.

199
00:17:37,900 --> 00:17:40,200
Said he'd promised my dad.

200
00:17:40,770 --> 00:17:44,070
And when we got home, my dad invited him to dinner.

201
00:17:44,300 --> 00:17:45,700
Because Din likes Star.

202
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:46,830
Plus one.

203
00:17:46,830 --> 00:17:47,670
Time!

204
00:17:48,030 --> 00:17:51,100
But yesterday Dad and Din talked for ages,

205
00:17:51,100 --> 00:17:52,630
I could barely get a word in.

206
00:17:52,900 --> 00:17:53,970
Right up Dad's alley.

207
00:17:53,970 --> 00:17:54,900
Exactly.

208
00:18:01,700 --> 00:18:03,530
Let me take a breather.

209
00:18:06,100 --> 00:18:07,700
Or maybe...

210
00:18:08,430 --> 00:18:10,170
I don't want to think it,

211
00:18:10,900 --> 00:18:13,970
but I think you like Star.

212
00:18:13,970 --> 00:18:17,430
And say Din does start hitting on you,

213
00:18:17,430 --> 00:18:20,100
what would our dear Star do?

214
00:18:24,330 --> 00:18:25,670
Stop the nonsense.

215
00:18:26,230 --> 00:18:29,870
I promised his dad. Taking him home is normal, right?

216
00:18:30,900 --> 00:18:32,470
You definitely like him.

217
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,070
Quit stirring.

218
00:18:35,670 --> 00:18:36,930
He doesn't like me.

219
00:18:37,200 --> 00:18:38,670
Din doesn't like me.

220
00:18:39,530 --> 00:18:40,600
The end.

221
00:18:41,500 --> 00:18:43,170
Go on, go study.

222
00:18:43,170 --> 00:18:44,770
Ugh, what a drag.

223
00:18:49,400 --> 00:18:51,200
Talking to you guys gives me a headache.

224
00:18:51,700 --> 00:18:54,530
So what's the deal? Huh?

225
00:18:54,970 --> 00:18:56,930
Did you talk to Kim?

226
00:18:56,930 --> 00:19:00,870
He writes great scripts, even wins contests,

227
00:19:00,870 --> 00:19:03,630
but he doesn't open up to people easily.

228
00:19:03,630 --> 00:19:07,100
Yeah, I did. He said to meet in the meeting room after class.

229
00:19:07,700 --> 00:19:10,600
Good. And watch what you say.

230
00:19:10,600 --> 00:19:11,300
Yeah.

231
00:19:13,070 --> 00:19:15,400
Does he want our help with anything?

232
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,200
He does.

233
00:19:19,070 --> 00:19:21,670
Listen carefully.

234
00:19:22,200 --> 00:19:25,300
He says the lead has to be you, no one else.

235
00:19:25,670 --> 00:19:27,900
The school's Thai dance prodigy.

236
00:19:27,900 --> 00:19:28,930
What!

237
00:19:28,930 --> 00:19:31,870
What? What do you want me to do?

238
00:19:31,870 --> 00:19:33,600
Be in the stage play.

239
00:19:33,600 --> 00:19:36,070
Whoa, no way.

240
00:19:36,070 --> 00:19:37,830
Ask someone else.

241
00:19:38,370 --> 00:19:39,770
Or how about Physics?

242
00:19:40,400 --> 00:19:41,700
Huh? Me?

243
00:19:41,700 --> 00:19:43,800
Physics can't do it.

244
00:19:44,270 --> 00:19:47,970
What would it take for you to do it, Fuen?

245
00:19:51,200 --> 00:19:55,630
Okay, if you want me in it, you have to cast someone close to me too.

246
00:19:56,270 --> 00:19:59,400
Or I won't do it even if it kills me.

247
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:03,370
It's a khon story, too. A school legend. It's hard.

248
00:20:03,370 --> 00:20:05,670
I knew you'd say that.

249
00:20:05,670 --> 00:20:06,830
But don't worry.

250
00:20:06,830 --> 00:20:08,670
I've got it all planned.

251
00:20:11,000 --> 00:20:15,400
My play isn't pure khon. It's contemporary Thai.

252
00:20:15,400 --> 00:20:19,070
And besides, your co-star is Din.

253
00:20:24,800 --> 00:20:27,730
See you in the main hall after class.

254
00:20:36,970 --> 00:20:38,570
Did I just mess up?

255
00:20:39,200 --> 00:20:43,300
Why does it feel like he had this all planned?

256
00:20:45,130 --> 00:20:47,900
So what role did he give you?

257
00:20:49,930 --> 00:20:51,330
Lord Thapfah.

258
00:20:53,930 --> 00:20:56,000
Go tell him now. I'll play opposite you.

259
00:20:56,000 --> 00:20:57,430
Bro...

260
00:21:00,800 --> 00:21:02,270
Um, so...

261
00:21:02,270 --> 00:21:04,400
There's something I want to talk about.

262
00:21:05,500 --> 00:21:06,300
Mm.

263
00:21:07,470 --> 00:21:09,970
But promise you won't get mad.

264
00:21:12,000 --> 00:21:12,800
Mm.

265
00:21:13,670 --> 00:21:14,530
Promise.

266
00:21:15,170 --> 00:21:16,500
Are you telling me or not?

267
00:21:16,500 --> 00:21:17,600
I am.

268
00:21:19,470 --> 00:21:20,830
It's about Aof...

269
00:21:20,830 --> 00:21:21,930
Chemi.

270
00:21:23,230 --> 00:21:27,970
Bro, I know I'm making you worry.

271
00:21:28,800 --> 00:21:33,800
But I promise if anything happens,

272
00:21:34,530 --> 00:21:37,700
I'll put myself first.

273
00:21:40,400 --> 00:21:42,870
And if I feel like I'm going to get hurt,

274
00:21:42,870 --> 00:21:45,030
I'll get myself out right away.

275
00:21:49,070 --> 00:21:58,630
Bro... give me one more chance, please?

276
00:22:03,970 --> 00:22:05,430
Okay, okay. Fine.

277
00:22:07,000 --> 00:22:08,300
You're not mad?

278
00:22:08,300 --> 00:22:10,070
I am. / What?

279
00:22:10,070 --> 00:22:12,370
If you don't keep your promise to me.

280
00:22:13,700 --> 00:22:15,130
Got it.

281
00:22:41,700 --> 00:22:43,530
Be firm about it.

282
00:22:43,530 --> 00:22:45,200
No means no.

283
00:22:49,000 --> 00:22:51,600
Yeah, trust me.

284
00:23:07,470 --> 00:23:09,470
Guys!

285
00:23:15,370 --> 00:23:16,830
I...

286
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:18,730
I...

287
00:23:25,830 --> 00:23:27,630
What do I have to do?

288
00:23:40,100 --> 00:23:42,300
If you don't want to do it, just tell me.

289
00:23:42,570 --> 00:23:45,300
I only just found out he wants us to play opposite each other.

290
00:23:45,630 --> 00:23:47,070
You can't, Fuen.

291
00:23:48,270 --> 00:23:51,030
This role fits you best.

292
00:23:56,100 --> 00:23:56,970
Oh, Din.

293
00:23:56,970 --> 00:23:58,030
Hey.

294
00:23:58,630 --> 00:23:59,730
I'm heading home.

295
00:23:59,730 --> 00:24:01,330
Hey, wish me luck.

296
00:24:02,800 --> 00:24:04,070
Yeah, yeah. Thanks.

297
00:24:05,630 --> 00:24:06,870
These guys are so forgetful.

298
00:24:06,870 --> 00:24:07,730
Yeah, I'm off.

299
00:24:07,730 --> 00:24:08,630
See ya.

300
00:24:17,970 --> 00:24:19,800
Tuck your shirt in, man.

301
00:24:19,800 --> 00:24:20,670
Oh, okay.

302
00:24:32,730 --> 00:24:35,170
Fuen, just do it.

303
00:24:35,170 --> 00:24:36,570
I don't want to rethink this.

304
00:24:36,970 --> 00:24:38,630
I saw you present in class once.

305
00:24:39,270 --> 00:24:40,730
You bluff like a pro.

306
00:24:40,730 --> 00:24:41,930
I don't bluff.

307
00:24:42,370 --> 00:24:43,170
True.

308
00:24:43,600 --> 00:24:47,170
Even if you forget your lines, you'll still wing it.

309
00:24:58,870 --> 00:25:01,300
Don't worry. I'll sort it out with him.

310
00:25:01,300 --> 00:25:02,300
Din,

311
00:25:02,800 --> 00:25:05,530
I think we should let Fuen decide.

312
00:25:17,170 --> 00:25:19,230
Physics, Physics.

313
00:25:23,400 --> 00:25:25,930
Give me a minute.

314
00:25:32,470 --> 00:25:33,270
Wow.

315
00:25:34,130 --> 00:25:35,800
Standing still like a boy band.

316
00:25:36,370 --> 00:25:38,070
Want a part?

317
00:25:44,700 --> 00:25:46,430
Hey, everyone, back to work.

318
00:26:06,630 --> 00:26:08,200
Chemi, listen to me.

319
00:26:09,600 --> 00:26:12,030
Let me take care of you again.

320
00:26:13,000 --> 00:26:16,470
I promise this time I'll do my best.

321
00:26:17,300 --> 00:26:19,830
And I won't be unkind to you anymore.

322
00:26:23,770 --> 00:26:24,630
Aof.

323
00:26:24,630 --> 00:26:26,600
Don't turn me down yet.

324
00:26:26,600 --> 00:26:28,130
Well... / It's not that.

325
00:26:29,770 --> 00:26:34,570
I just... wanted to say...

326
00:26:35,800 --> 00:26:39,300
what you said just now... was better than what you wrote.

327
00:26:42,430 --> 00:26:43,630
And...

328
00:26:47,370 --> 00:26:49,600
I'll give you another chance.

329
00:26:55,900 --> 00:26:57,300
Yay!

330
00:26:57,830 --> 00:26:59,170
Really, Chemi?

331
00:26:59,670 --> 00:27:00,770
You mean it, right?

332
00:27:00,770 --> 00:27:01,730
There are people around.

333
00:27:02,230 --> 00:27:03,730
You're really giving me a chance?

334
00:27:03,730 --> 00:27:04,830
Get down. You're heavy.

335
00:27:07,530 --> 00:27:11,030
Sorry if I got a little too excited.

336
00:27:11,930 --> 00:27:14,430
I thought you'd never give me another chance.

337
00:27:18,870 --> 00:27:24,570
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

338
00:27:24,570 --> 00:27:30,670
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

339
00:27:40,030 --> 00:27:42,270
It's only been one day.

340
00:27:43,770 --> 00:27:46,970
I waited four years for you.

341
00:27:47,600 --> 00:27:50,360
♪ Because of you, a world that was all noise ♪

342
00:27:50,360 --> 00:27:55,020
♪ showed someone who was lost the way to his own heart ♪

343
00:27:55,020 --> 00:27:56,300
♪ all I've searched for ♪

344
00:27:56,300 --> 00:27:58,170
Thank you, Chemi.

345
00:27:58,170 --> 00:28:03,100
♪ Every question in my heart has an answer now ♪

346
00:28:03,100 --> 00:28:08,800
♪ No matter how the story goes, in the end my answer is you ♪

347
00:28:08,800 --> 00:28:11,300
Take good care of me.

348
00:28:23,330 --> 00:28:26,900
Will you tell me now why you don't want me in it?

349
00:28:29,530 --> 00:28:31,630
It's written all over your face.

350
00:28:31,630 --> 00:28:33,770
Something's definitely up.

351
00:28:40,830 --> 00:28:42,930
There's a kiss scene.

352
00:28:42,930 --> 00:28:44,500
Didn't you read the script?

353
00:28:44,500 --> 00:28:46,430
What! Seriously?

354
00:28:48,430 --> 00:28:50,400
Mm.

355
00:28:50,400 --> 00:28:55,200
And how could I stand watching you kiss someone else?

356
00:28:55,200 --> 00:28:58,370
And it's Din, of all people.

357
00:29:01,370 --> 00:29:03,900
I don't feel anything for Din anymore.

358
00:29:04,530 --> 00:29:07,430
And Din's already given up on me.

359
00:29:08,200 --> 00:29:10,030
Fuen.

360
00:29:10,670 --> 00:29:14,270
If you were me,

361
00:29:15,130 --> 00:29:16,900
how would you feel?

362
00:29:17,500 --> 00:29:18,900
Come on, tell me.

363
00:29:31,030 --> 00:29:34,730
Din and I really are just friends now.

364
00:29:42,900 --> 00:29:46,030
You want to do it that badly?

365
00:29:49,070 --> 00:29:51,370
If I don't do it,

366
00:29:51,900 --> 00:29:54,370
won't I look selfish?

367
00:29:55,400 --> 00:29:58,300
I admit it. I want to do it.

368
00:29:59,530 --> 00:30:04,700
But I'm not sure I can pull it off.

369
00:30:16,500 --> 00:30:18,600
Whatever you set your mind to,

370
00:30:18,600 --> 00:30:20,870
you always pull it off.

371
00:30:25,000 --> 00:30:28,700
Do it. I'm fine.

372
00:30:36,000 --> 00:30:37,570
Physics.

373
00:30:43,530 --> 00:30:45,200
Really?

374
00:30:45,200 --> 00:30:46,530
For real?

375
00:30:47,430 --> 00:30:49,800
Yeah, really, it's fine.

376
00:30:51,900 --> 00:30:53,930
Really? / Hey.

377
00:30:54,730 --> 00:30:56,970
It's fine. Really.

378
00:31:04,500 --> 00:31:06,730
Physics.

379
00:31:10,530 --> 00:31:12,630
I have an answer for you now.

380
00:31:13,270 --> 00:31:14,970
Just hang on a little longer.

381
00:31:15,730 --> 00:31:18,670
I want to see the fireworks with you too.

382
00:31:36,000 --> 00:31:40,700
So give it your all, okay?

383
00:31:44,530 --> 00:31:45,930
Go.

384
00:32:03,030 --> 00:32:04,300
Physics!

385
00:32:04,930 --> 00:32:06,770
Come here so I can kick you.

386
00:32:07,670 --> 00:32:08,470
Hey.

387
00:32:25,430 --> 00:32:26,730
Kim,

388
00:32:28,630 --> 00:32:31,930
I'm not sure I can do this well,

389
00:32:33,900 --> 00:32:35,670
but I'll try.

390
00:32:37,800 --> 00:32:40,430
Yes, Lord Thapfah.

391
00:33:00,300 --> 00:33:01,470
I'm beat today.

392
00:33:01,470 --> 00:33:02,970
Yeah, today was exhausting.

393
00:33:03,230 --> 00:33:05,920
Want to grab dessert before tutoring?

394
00:33:05,920 --> 00:33:06,630
Sure.

395
00:33:06,630 --> 00:33:07,970
Coming? / Let's go.

396
00:33:08,470 --> 00:33:09,570
What should we get?

397
00:33:11,770 --> 00:33:13,300
Star... it's Rei.

398
00:33:14,530 --> 00:33:15,530
Star!

399
00:33:15,530 --> 00:33:16,670
Rei.

400
00:33:17,370 --> 00:33:19,730
What are you doing here?

401
00:33:20,070 --> 00:33:21,970
You've got tutoring, right?

402
00:33:21,970 --> 00:33:24,930
I want to talk. Let me take you.

403
00:33:29,200 --> 00:33:33,370
Please, Star. I really need your advice.

404
00:33:33,870 --> 00:33:35,130
Okay.

405
00:33:37,730 --> 00:33:40,600
I'll go on ahead, then.

406
00:33:41,870 --> 00:33:42,670
Yeah.

407
00:33:50,270 --> 00:33:51,500
What do we do?

408
00:33:51,500 --> 00:33:52,830
Ask the group chat for help.

409
00:33:52,830 --> 00:33:53,800
Go on.

410
00:33:56,130 --> 00:33:57,870
Guys, we've got a problem.

411
00:33:58,230 --> 00:33:59,730
Rei took Star away.

412
00:33:59,730 --> 00:34:00,980
"WTF, where?" / "You lost him?"

413
00:34:00,980 --> 00:34:02,790
"Does Time know?" / "Now what?" / "Send Din!"

414
00:34:02,790 --> 00:34:04,400
"Din's at the play." / "Mission! Think!"

415
00:34:04,400 --> 00:34:06,770
"Who can go look?" / "I'll send Din. Booboo, Tue, go look."

416
00:34:12,600 --> 00:34:16,570
Why do you share this seat with me?

417
00:34:16,570 --> 00:34:18,600
It is my duty to guard you,

418
00:34:18,600 --> 00:34:20,870
so I must stay as close to you as I can, must I not?

419
00:34:21,400 --> 00:34:23,370
Where else would you have me be?

420
00:34:33,500 --> 00:34:34,600
Cut.

421
00:34:35,070 --> 00:34:38,530
Oh, damn.

422
00:34:38,770 --> 00:34:41,600
My heart was racing. I was so tense.

423
00:34:42,230 --> 00:34:46,100
Sorry, Din. I flubbed it so many times and wasted your time.

424
00:34:46,100 --> 00:34:49,730
It's fine. I'm just grateful you agreed to help.

425
00:34:50,230 --> 00:34:52,530
You guys are amazing.

426
00:34:53,130 --> 00:34:55,530
Oh, Din, can we talk?

427
00:34:55,530 --> 00:34:56,870
Sure.

428
00:35:08,000 --> 00:35:09,170
So?

429
00:35:09,170 --> 00:35:10,800
How was that?

430
00:35:12,170 --> 00:35:15,230
Good. Told you you could do it.

431
00:35:17,400 --> 00:35:18,700
Give me your hand.

432
00:35:18,700 --> 00:35:20,300
I'm hungry.

433
00:35:20,970 --> 00:35:23,430
But no one's home today.

434
00:35:23,430 --> 00:35:25,130
Come cook for me.

435
00:35:27,500 --> 00:35:28,730
Sure.

436
00:35:30,700 --> 00:35:32,870
Uh, guys.

437
00:35:33,670 --> 00:35:34,730
Kim,

438
00:35:35,130 --> 00:35:36,330
rehearsal's over, right?

439
00:35:36,330 --> 00:35:37,200
Yes.

440
00:35:37,200 --> 00:35:38,430
I'll head out first.

441
00:35:38,430 --> 00:35:39,330
Oh, sure.

442
00:35:49,670 --> 00:35:51,370
Where's Din rushing off to?

443
00:35:51,800 --> 00:35:53,330
A mission.

444
00:35:53,830 --> 00:35:54,770
Oh.

445
00:35:55,970 --> 00:35:59,330
Time, dear, I think we need to talk.

446
00:35:59,730 --> 00:36:01,770
I've been waiting to talk to you guys too.

447
00:36:02,600 --> 00:36:03,970
I want to know too.

448
00:36:03,970 --> 00:36:05,230
Sure.

449
00:36:05,230 --> 00:36:07,070
The more help, the better.

450
00:36:08,500 --> 00:36:09,700
So here's the thing.

451
00:36:09,970 --> 00:36:13,200
"Mission 2: Save Star from Rei"

452
00:36:28,100 --> 00:36:29,770
Are you hungry, Chemi?

453
00:36:32,630 --> 00:36:35,930
A little.

454
00:36:36,870 --> 00:36:38,570
What about you, Aof?

455
00:36:38,570 --> 00:36:39,900
I'm getting hungry.

456
00:36:41,270 --> 00:36:44,200
Want to find something to eat?

457
00:36:44,730 --> 00:36:46,830
Let's try this place, Chemi.

458
00:36:51,600 --> 00:36:54,070
This place is going viral right now.

459
00:36:54,070 --> 00:36:57,030
I've wanted to try it for ages. Let's go.

460
00:36:57,570 --> 00:36:58,730
Okay.

461
00:36:59,500 --> 00:37:02,030
If you want it, let's go.

462
00:37:04,730 --> 00:37:07,300
Welcome to Gentia Cafe!

463
00:37:10,170 --> 00:37:11,900
What would you like, Aof?

464
00:37:13,070 --> 00:37:14,630
You order first, Chemi.

465
00:37:15,900 --> 00:37:20,730
I'll have a Matcha Sommerso, less sweet.

466
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:26,870
And I'll have a Truffle Milk Sommerso, extra, extra sweet.

467
00:37:28,400 --> 00:37:30,330
Sweet tooth, huh?

468
00:37:39,970 --> 00:37:42,170
You want this one, Chemi?

469
00:37:47,170 --> 00:37:51,030
Excuse me, how do I get this promotion?

470
00:37:51,030 --> 00:37:54,470
Spend 2,000 baht. You need 1,760 more.

471
00:37:54,470 --> 00:37:56,900
Then I'll take anything to make it 2,000.

472
00:37:56,900 --> 00:37:58,270
Wow, sure.

473
00:38:15,370 --> 00:38:17,470
Oh, thank you.

474
00:38:22,900 --> 00:38:24,570
One sec.

475
00:38:26,530 --> 00:38:28,230
Smile, Chemi.

476
00:38:46,600 --> 00:38:48,670
One each for us to keep.

477
00:38:49,570 --> 00:38:51,130
Thank you.

478
00:38:56,430 --> 00:38:58,770
Hello, feel free to look around.

479
00:38:58,770 --> 00:39:00,570
We have a new collection in.

480
00:39:13,170 --> 00:39:14,570
Like it?

481
00:39:17,070 --> 00:39:19,000
No, just...

482
00:39:19,000 --> 00:39:21,530
it's pretty, and it's the new collection.

483
00:39:21,870 --> 00:39:22,970
Thank you.

484
00:39:22,970 --> 00:39:24,000
Let's go.

485
00:39:24,300 --> 00:39:25,030
Excuse me.

486
00:39:25,030 --> 00:39:26,900
Two of these, please.

487
00:39:27,300 --> 00:39:28,830
400 baht. / Sure.

488
00:39:29,300 --> 00:39:30,030
Here.

489
00:39:30,030 --> 00:39:30,970
Thank you. One moment.

490
00:39:31,330 --> 00:39:32,170
Sure.

491
00:39:41,200 --> 00:39:44,700
Aof, can we take it slow?

492
00:39:45,130 --> 00:39:48,300
I don't want you pushing yourself too hard.

493
00:39:48,300 --> 00:39:50,000
You'll wear yourself out.

494
00:39:50,000 --> 00:39:51,430
I'm not tired.

495
00:39:51,430 --> 00:39:53,000
Because I'm not even trying.

496
00:39:54,570 --> 00:39:57,470
I told you, this time I'll do my best.

497
00:40:09,330 --> 00:40:13,530
For me, this is nothing.

498
00:40:23,670 --> 00:40:24,730
Cute, right?

499
00:40:54,070 --> 00:40:56,000
What are you looking at, Aof?

500
00:40:57,370 --> 00:40:59,170
Oh, nothing.

501
00:41:00,470 --> 00:41:02,970
Let's get going. Come on.

502
00:41:04,200 --> 00:41:06,030
What do you want to eat, Chemi?

503
00:41:07,300 --> 00:41:08,430
Noodles.

504
00:41:08,430 --> 00:41:10,270
Noodles? / Yup.

505
00:41:11,030 --> 00:41:12,570
That place?

506
00:41:21,300 --> 00:41:23,430
You can drop me here, Rei.

507
00:41:24,330 --> 00:41:25,870
You don't want me to walk you in?

508
00:41:26,230 --> 00:41:28,230
I need to hurry to class.

509
00:41:28,230 --> 00:41:31,300
And honestly, if this is all you want to talk about,

510
00:41:31,300 --> 00:41:32,900
you can just call me.

511
00:41:35,070 --> 00:41:37,000
Am I making you uncomfortable, Star?

512
00:41:38,370 --> 00:41:41,000
I know what you're thinking, Rei.

513
00:41:41,430 --> 00:41:43,970
But you're really just a big brother to me.

514
00:41:44,430 --> 00:41:47,270
I don't think it can be more than that.

515
00:41:49,230 --> 00:41:52,400
I get it. Go to class.

516
00:41:52,600 --> 00:41:54,330
I'll keep my distance.

517
00:41:56,070 --> 00:41:57,930
I'll go to class, then.

518
00:42:06,830 --> 00:42:07,930
Si.

519
00:42:09,930 --> 00:42:13,130
Hey, Si, did you buy this for me?

520
00:42:15,100 --> 00:42:17,370
Huh? I didn't buy it.

521
00:42:19,200 --> 00:42:20,270
Huh?

522
00:42:21,930 --> 00:42:24,030
Then whose is this?

523
00:42:24,030 --> 00:42:26,200
It was already here when I got here.

524
00:42:26,200 --> 00:42:28,470
I thought you'd gotten here first, Star.

525
00:42:39,630 --> 00:42:41,830
See you, Star. Thanks for the snacks.

526
00:42:41,830 --> 00:42:43,830
Bye-bye. Enjoy.

527
00:42:49,870 --> 00:42:50,670
Hey.

528
00:42:54,300 --> 00:42:56,470
Could someone open the door?

529
00:42:59,670 --> 00:43:01,370
Is anyone out there?

530
00:43:12,900 --> 00:43:15,430
Oh? / Star.

531
00:43:22,000 --> 00:43:23,570
Did something happen in there?

532
00:43:24,730 --> 00:43:28,000
Nothing, Din. I was just in a hurry.

533
00:43:28,600 --> 00:43:30,200
Everyone's gone home.

534
00:43:30,200 --> 00:43:33,170
And the lights around here aren't great, Din.

535
00:43:36,430 --> 00:43:37,600
You sure?

536
00:43:38,870 --> 00:43:42,530
I'm sure. So, did you come for something?

537
00:43:43,070 --> 00:43:45,300
Um, I'm hungry.

538
00:43:45,700 --> 00:43:48,500
Didn't you say you'd treat me to a meal?

539
00:43:48,900 --> 00:43:50,370
Today?

540
00:43:50,370 --> 00:43:51,090
Mm.

541
00:43:51,430 --> 00:43:53,130
So I came to find you.

542
00:43:53,530 --> 00:43:57,300
Oh. What do you want to eat?

543
00:43:57,570 --> 00:44:00,900
Let's walk around. Whichever place has the fewest people.

544
00:44:04,500 --> 00:44:07,100
Then let's hurry, Din.

545
00:44:35,570 --> 00:44:37,370
Here to help or get in the way?

546
00:44:38,770 --> 00:44:43,000
I want to help, but I'm scared I'll mess it up.

547
00:44:53,100 --> 00:44:56,070
First, pull the leaves off like this.

548
00:44:59,100 --> 00:45:00,530
And when you chop them,

549
00:45:02,470 --> 00:45:05,830
not too small, or they'll go mushy when boiled.

550
00:45:10,500 --> 00:45:11,800
Trust me.

551
00:45:13,600 --> 00:45:14,870
Every time you say that,

552
00:45:15,870 --> 00:45:17,700
I get nervous.

553
00:45:17,700 --> 00:45:19,230
Last time,

554
00:45:19,230 --> 00:45:20,930
you climbed through Star's window.

555
00:45:21,130 --> 00:45:22,230
This time,

556
00:45:23,130 --> 00:45:26,130
are you going to blow up cabbage in your kitchen?

557
00:45:27,200 --> 00:45:29,270
There's something I want to know.

558
00:45:32,430 --> 00:45:35,630
You never liked anyone before hitting on me?

559
00:45:54,000 --> 00:45:57,630
If I said never, would you believe me?

560
00:46:08,770 --> 00:46:12,930
I would, because you've never lied to me.

561
00:46:16,600 --> 00:46:18,300
Let's keep going.

562
00:46:24,730 --> 00:46:26,000
Want to try?

563
00:46:26,300 --> 00:46:28,070
You can eat this?

564
00:46:28,670 --> 00:46:30,330
Not yet.

565
00:46:30,330 --> 00:46:31,970
Or you can eat it raw.

566
00:46:31,970 --> 00:46:33,330
It's usually boiled first.

567
00:46:33,330 --> 00:46:34,570
Here, keep chopping.

568
00:46:55,400 --> 00:46:56,530
Star.

569
00:47:05,630 --> 00:47:10,500
Do you know why I came today?

570
00:47:13,070 --> 00:47:15,030
For a mission, probably.

571
00:47:17,470 --> 00:47:19,570
I'd be lying if I said it wasn't.

572
00:47:20,370 --> 00:47:22,700
Because Time really did give me a mission.

573
00:47:23,070 --> 00:47:26,230
I think you should stop doing the missions.

574
00:47:27,470 --> 00:47:30,770
If you want my contact, I'll give it to you right now.

575
00:47:30,770 --> 00:47:31,800
Why?

576
00:47:32,470 --> 00:47:34,630
Are you upset with me about something?

577
00:47:35,970 --> 00:47:40,570
No, I just don't want you doing these missions anymore.

578
00:47:43,370 --> 00:47:45,370
Can I know why?

579
00:47:46,530 --> 00:47:49,700
If it makes sense, I'll stop.

580
00:47:51,200 --> 00:47:52,770
I have feelings for you.

581
00:47:55,930 --> 00:47:57,430
You might not even realize it,

582
00:47:57,430 --> 00:48:02,230
but your kindness makes me get my hopes up.

583
00:48:02,870 --> 00:48:07,200
And I don't trust myself if you stay this close to me.

584
00:48:08,530 --> 00:48:10,500
Since when?

585
00:48:15,470 --> 00:48:17,700
All the time.

586
00:48:22,770 --> 00:48:25,370
When you peeled shrimp for me.

587
00:48:34,630 --> 00:48:37,070
When you saved me from drowning.

588
00:48:50,700 --> 00:48:53,200
When you took care of me.

589
00:48:57,000 --> 00:48:59,570
And right now, too.

590
00:49:07,470 --> 00:49:11,270
At first I didn't even know how I felt.

591
00:49:12,200 --> 00:49:16,570
When my friends said I was acting weird, I didn't think much of it.

592
00:49:19,730 --> 00:49:22,070
Until you told me straight,

593
00:49:23,130 --> 00:49:27,830
then I realized... why I'm here.

594
00:49:34,000 --> 00:49:35,070
Star.

595
00:49:39,000 --> 00:49:41,630
I have feelings for you too.

596
00:49:56,130 --> 00:49:58,630
I'm happy when I do nice things for you.

597
00:50:02,300 --> 00:50:05,930
So let me keep doing the missions.

598
00:50:08,100 --> 00:50:11,600
And can I add one more rule between us?

599
00:50:14,170 --> 00:50:15,630
What is it?

600
00:50:16,770 --> 00:50:19,800
If something I do makes you happy,

601
00:50:20,600 --> 00:50:24,370
add some letters for me, based on how you feel.

602
00:50:26,170 --> 00:50:27,470
It may not be like...

603
00:50:28,370 --> 00:50:30,330
collecting stars in kindergarten,

604
00:50:31,730 --> 00:50:33,730
but if they're stars from Star,

605
00:50:34,630 --> 00:50:36,570
I'd be really proud.

606
00:50:45,830 --> 00:50:47,070
Sure.

607
00:50:48,200 --> 00:50:50,670
So how many letters do I have now?

608
00:51:43,470 --> 00:51:45,930
Keep up the quality, okay?

609
00:51:45,930 --> 00:51:47,330
Yes.

610
00:51:48,200 --> 00:51:50,000
There's a long way to go,

611
00:51:50,930 --> 00:51:53,100
but I'll help you,

612
00:51:53,100 --> 00:51:54,800
and stay by your side.

613
00:51:57,400 --> 00:51:59,700
Get home safe.

614
00:52:07,630 --> 00:52:09,200
Dad!

615
00:52:09,200 --> 00:52:13,330
How long are you going to stand there? The mosquitoes are eating me alive.

616
00:52:14,800 --> 00:52:18,300
If you're going to flirt, do it inside.

617
00:52:18,300 --> 00:52:19,870
Dad!

618
00:52:21,100 --> 00:52:23,070
Hello, sir.

619
00:52:24,200 --> 00:52:25,470
Wait inside.

620
00:52:25,470 --> 00:52:26,370
Okay.

621
00:52:53,170 --> 00:52:54,770
What are you doing?

622
00:52:57,070 --> 00:52:58,530
Nice bracelet.

623
00:52:59,070 --> 00:52:59,900
Is it?

624
00:52:59,900 --> 00:53:01,430
Someone bought it for me.

625
00:53:03,300 --> 00:53:04,800
Not that I'm bragging.

626
00:53:12,900 --> 00:53:14,870
Thanks for walking me home.

627
00:53:15,370 --> 00:53:18,300
Let me know when you get home.

628
00:53:18,300 --> 00:53:19,500
Shure fing~

629
00:53:20,700 --> 00:53:21,830
Sure thing.

630
00:53:21,830 --> 00:53:23,870
Mm, that's it. Correct.

631
00:53:24,900 --> 00:53:26,700
You're funny these days.

632
00:53:27,500 --> 00:53:30,400
Mm, I'm going.

633
00:53:32,570 --> 00:53:33,700
Bye-bye.

634
00:53:33,700 --> 00:53:34,830
Bye.

635
00:53:37,200 --> 00:53:38,770
Chemi,

636
00:53:39,900 --> 00:53:43,200
bad dreams bring ghosts, sweet dreams bring me.

637
00:53:47,470 --> 00:53:49,400
Get home safe. It's late.

638
00:54:14,830 --> 00:54:15,970
Hello, Mii.

639
00:54:15,970 --> 00:54:17,200
What's up, Aof?

640
00:54:18,970 --> 00:54:20,700
Come out and see me.

641
00:54:21,270 --> 00:54:23,430
There's something I need to talk to you about.

642
00:54:32,600 --> 00:54:33,970
"You're scared of being let down."

643
00:54:33,970 --> 00:54:35,700
"Deep down, you trust Aof with him." (Fuen)

644
00:54:35,700 --> 00:54:37,700
"I thought that once, and got let down." (Physics)

645
00:54:37,700 --> 00:54:42,100
"Don't worry, there's a long way to go, but I'll help you and stay by your side." (Star)

646
00:54:42,100 --> 00:54:43,630
"Thanks, Physics. Don't worry."

647
00:54:43,630 --> 00:54:45,130
"I'll choose what's best for me."

648
00:54:45,130 --> 00:54:47,270
"If I get hurt, I'll get over it. Trust me." (Chemi)

649
00:54:47,570 --> 00:54:48,830
If Fuen and Din agree,

650
00:54:48,830 --> 00:54:51,700
as actors, they should give it their all.

651
00:54:52,770 --> 00:54:53,970
Din.

652
00:54:56,630 --> 00:54:58,970
I know you take good care of yourself, Time,

653
00:54:58,970 --> 00:55:00,800
but let me take even better care of you.

654
00:55:00,800 --> 00:55:03,000
You don't have to believe my words, Chemi.

655
00:55:03,000 --> 00:55:04,730
Just watch what I do.

656
00:55:05,930 --> 00:55:09,700
Didn't you tell me to trust your actions?

657
00:55:09,700 --> 00:55:13,070
If I don't lie to you, you'll leave me, right?

658
00:55:16,000 --> 00:55:18,200
Then just leave me.
